%% F6--F7: Interventions and cross-environment
%% ============================================================

\subsection{F6--F7: Interventions and Multiple Pathways}
\label{sec:f6}

\paragraph{F6: $\dt{=}1$ imagination does not prevent all collapse.}
Exp\_008e\_v3 restricts imagination to $\dt{=}1$ while retaining the trained embedding. Seed~1 is healthy (eval 869.9, $\nve = 0.94\times$); seed~2 collapses (eval $715 \rightarrow 137$, $\nve = 3.78\times$), but via a qualitatively distinct mechanism (Figure~\ref{fig:multiple_pathways}). Classic CIVO (008d, Pathway~A) shows value explosion followed by evaluation decline with decreasing entropy; 008e\_v3\_s2 (Pathway~B) shows evaluation crash with \emph{increasing} entropy ($-5.21 \rightarrow -3.83$) while values remain stable. This produces the sole false positive in the NVE classification.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.65\columnwidth]{figures/paper/fig6_multiple_pathways.pdf}
\caption{Contrasting collapse dynamics. \textbf{Left:} 008d (CIVO), value explosion with entropy decrease. \textbf{Right:} 008e\_v3 s2 (non-CIVO), evaluation crash with entropy increase.}
\label{fig:multiple_pathways}
\end{figure}

\paragraph{F7: Full-pathway gradient stopping shows mixed results.}
Exp\_018 applies Selective Gradient Stopping (SGS) by detaching all non-KL gradients from $e_{\dt}$, blocking the observation decoder pathway identified in F2 as the primary CIVO conduit. Figure~\ref{fig:civo_decomposition} decomposes evaluation returns across conditions. Trained $\dt$-embedding alone produces $-73\%$ peak and $-86\%$ final eval degradation relative to the baseline. Full-SGS seed~1 avoids collapse (eval \sgseval{}, $-51\%$ final relative to baseline) while seed~2 collapses (eval 40.8, $-96\%$), yielding a 50\% prevention rate. SGS reduces but does not eliminate CIVO risk: the gradient pathway it blocks is necessary but not sufficient for reliable prevention. Reward-only SGS (016e) fails entirely (NVE $10.42\times$). Cross-environment validation on Cheetah Run (010b) confirms CIVO generalization: evaluation peaks at 321.9 before declining to 51.7 at 105K ($-84\%$, minimum 22.7 at 65K); peak NVE $14.59\times$.

